# Sub-tick interpolation of the homeworld portal preview's aperture
# (scripts/check_portal_subtick.sh).
#   <bk2> | <V> | vertex=<x>,<y> ... [tol=<px>] [step=<px>] [judge=<a>,...]
# V is the canonical VBL the intermediate present at V+1 sits above; V-2 opens
# the interval that present covers. V is even because a tick spans two VBLs
# here: the intermediate present at V+1 has to fall inside V's own tick.
#
# The statistic is the aperture polygon's corners, read from the feeder's own
# emitted list, not a pixel mask: the aperture spans most of the frame.
# Spyro walks at the Sunny Villa portal and the aperture opens across these
# ticks. Each row names three corners of the aperture whose canonical step over
# the interval is well clear of the floor and that stand far apart from every
# other corner.
#
# The second row is the interval whose visible pentagon edge count drops, where
# the whole-set lerp gate used to disable interpolation for the present.
#
# The bound is 1.0 px: the rect is captured as integers and the aperture is
# their clip against the pentagon, so a corner's expected position carries the
# rounding of both.
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry.bk2 | 2530 | vertex=319.36,12 vertex=412,81 vertex=412,215 tol=1.0
sunrise-spring-sunny-villa-portal-entry.bk2 | 2534 | vertex=341.08,12 vertex=438,82 vertex=46,66 tol=1.0
